## reading
The default configuration is the fastest measured tonight and needs no change: social
chanseq lets the phone aggregate (3,536 joined frames) at 15.8% CRC instead of the 40.3%
seen when aggregating on fixed 149. With the Q38 netd (no software drops) it reaches
0.92 MB/s - close to the 1.12 MB/s historical best, which used the same configuration
with the old netd, so the remaining gap is run-to-run variance, not a regression.
Merge is therefore configuration-dependent, not universally bad: it must stay ON for
social and OFF for fixed. The supervisor default (social + merge) is correct.
Next: repeat this configuration 2-3 times for a median, then ship the Q38 netd in the
single-file package.
